00:15:07.773 --> 00:15:10.042 align:start size:97% position:3%
they're going in
interesting directions, too.

00:15:10.042 --> 00:15:12.478
But you know, to me,
I continue to believe

00:15:12.478 --> 00:15:14.680
that we have to think about
this as an antitrust problem.

00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:18.217 align:start size:97% position:3%
The technology companies are
individually too powerful

00:15:18.217 --> 00:15:21.287 align:start size:97% position:3%
within their markets, and
what they have ended up doing

00:15:21.287 --> 00:15:24.657 align:start size:97% position:3%
is imposing this ideological
regime from the top down.

00:15:24.657 --> 00:15:26.091
And look, this is
a little bit weird,

00:15:26.091 --> 00:15:27.293
I think, for a lot
of conservatives.

00:15:27.293 --> 00:15:28.761
- [Dave] Yep.

00:15:28.761 --> 00:15:29.428
- A lot of people who believe
in the free market, right?

00:15:29.428 --> 00:15:30.663
- [Dave] Yeah.

00:15:30.663 --> 00:15:32.164
- They say, well, these
are private companies.

00:15:32.164 --> 00:15:33.365
And my counter argument to
that, Dave, is always, well,

00:15:33.365 --> 00:15:34.600
they're private companies,

00:15:34.600 --> 00:15:36.201
but they've achieved
their market power

00:15:36.201 --> 00:15:39.438 align:start size:88% position:13%
through an unbelievable
accumulation of
government favors,

00:15:39.438 --> 00:15:42.141
of illegal carve outs,
of liability protections.

00:15:42.141 --> 00:15:44.243
So these are behemoths created

00:15:44.243 --> 00:15:45.978 align:start size:84% position:16%
by the power of the
US federal government,

00:15:45.978 --> 00:15:47.880 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I think they can
only be curtailed

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:49.648 align:start size:84% position:16%
by the power of the
US federal government.

00:15:49.648 --> 00:15:51.383
So, I really think
that the, you know,

00:15:51.383 --> 00:15:53.118
we need to go into
trust buster mode,

00:15:53.118 --> 00:15:56.121 align:start size:84% position:16%
break up some of
these companies, make
them less powerful.

00:15:56.121 --> 00:15:58.524
Some of this, even the
threat of antitrust,

00:15:58.524 --> 00:16:02.561
I think, is making these
companies less ideological

00:16:02.561 --> 00:16:04.296
and less progressive.

00:16:04.296 --> 00:16:07.032
Obviously Twitter is a, I
think, a really good thing.

00:16:07.032 --> 00:16:09.435
I think what Elon did
is frankly heroic.

00:16:09.435 --> 00:16:10.869
But you still have Facebook.

00:16:10.869 --> 00:16:12.104
You still have Google,

00:16:12.104 --> 00:16:13.772
which is probably the
single biggest problem.

00:16:13.772 --> 00:16:16.942 align:start size:97% position:3%
I think the threat of action
is making these companies

00:16:16.942 --> 00:16:18.877
a little bit less crazy,

00:16:18.877 --> 00:16:21.046
but I think real action
would restore some sanity

00:16:21.046 --> 00:16:22.581
to our process.

00:16:22.581 --> 00:16:24.416
One thing, and I know we're
a little short on time here,

00:16:24.416 --> 00:16:26.318
but one quick thing on this.

00:16:26.318 --> 00:16:29.588 align:start size:88% position:13%
So, the way that Google
is most powerful,

00:16:29.588 --> 00:16:32.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
you maybe have heard this,
so stop me if you had,

00:16:32.157 --> 00:16:34.259
is it really biases-

00:16:34.259 --> 00:16:36.028
- Other people are watching
this too, so, it's okay.

00:16:36.028 --> 00:16:37.196
- Okay. Sure.

00:16:37.196 --> 00:16:39.698 align:start size:84% position:16%
But it really
biases fundraising-

00:16:39.698 --> 00:16:40.632
- [Dave] Yeah.

00:16:40.632 --> 00:16:41.900
- To Democrats over Republicans.

00:16:41.900 --> 00:16:43.135
- [Dave] Yeah.

00:16:43.135 --> 00:16:44.370
- So if you look at
the way that Gmail

00:16:44.370 --> 00:16:45.904
filters Republican
fundraising emails-

00:16:45.904 --> 00:16:47.172
- [Dave] Yeah.

00:16:47.172 --> 00:16:48.374
- Versus Democratic
fundraising emails.

00:16:48.374 --> 00:16:49.641
I just went through
a campaign, man.

00:16:49.641 --> 00:16:51.276
That's how you pay for
the TV advertisements

00:16:51.276 --> 00:16:53.078
that reach the middle
of the road voters

00:16:53.078 --> 00:16:56.648
that every person needs,
even in a deep red state.

00:16:56.648 --> 00:17:01.053
So, if Google is biasing
their own email client-

00:17:01.053 --> 00:17:01.987
- [Dave] Yep.

00:17:01.987 --> 00:17:03.222
- To left wing activists,

00:17:03.222 --> 00:17:05.124
that's gonna have
major ramifications

00:17:05.124 --> 00:17:06.091
for our political system.

00:17:06.091 --> 00:17:07.326
I think it already has.

00:17:07.326 --> 00:17:08.660
I think it's one of
the reasons, frankly,

00:17:08.660 --> 00:17:09.928
Blake lost in Arizona.

00:17:09.928 --> 00:17:11.063
I think it's one of
the reasons Herschel

00:17:11.063 --> 00:17:12.564
didn't do as well in Georgia

00:17:12.564 --> 00:17:15.801 align:start size:88% position:13%
is because the
massive fundraising
advantage the left has.

00:17:15.801 --> 00:17:17.102
If you don't fix that problem,

00:17:17.102 --> 00:17:19.838
you can't send good
people to Washington.

00:17:19.838 --> 00:17:21.673 align:start size:84% position:16%
The best you're
gonna get is frankly

00:17:21.673 --> 00:17:24.076
establishment blow hards
who don't do anything.

00:17:24.076 --> 00:17:26.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
The worse you're gonna
get is far left Democrats.

00:17:26.512 --> 00:17:30.549
To actually have a real
America first movement,

00:17:30.549 --> 00:17:32.851
you have to solve the big
tech fundraising problem.

00:17:32.851 --> 00:17:34.119
- All right. This
was somewhat brief.

00:17:34.119 --> 00:17:35.220
- Okay.

00:17:35.220 --> 00:17:36.455 align:start size:88% position:13%
- But we'll do it again.
- Absolutely.

00:17:36.455 --> 00:17:37.956
- And my challenge to
you always will be that

00:17:37.956 --> 00:17:40.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
you gotta still be excited
when you walk in there.

00:17:40.192 --> 00:17:41.693
- Yeah.

00:17:41.693 --> 00:17:42.895
- Because I can sense a
lot of the people aren't,

00:17:42.895 --> 00:17:43.862
and that is part
of the problem, so.

00:17:43.862 --> 00:17:44.897
- Yeah, agreed. Thanks, Dave.

00:17:44.897 --> 00:17:46.365 align:start size:84% position:16%
Good to see you, man.
- Yeah.

